00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:20.200
Now, the business model canvas has nine
elements, but

00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:23.750
they have identified the first four that
you need to address.

00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:28.850
Now, once you have this the value
proposition is something that you test

00:05:28.850 --> 00:05:32.110
in your direct interaction of your user
with your prototype.

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:37.350
Through their reaction, what is the value
proposition that they see?

00:05:37.350 --> 00:05:39.700
Does it match your value proposition?

00:05:39.700 --> 00:05:41.310
The customer segment.

00:05:41.310 --> 00:05:43.230
Once you define your customer segment,

00:05:43.230 --> 00:05:48.860
the users that you talk to, must belong in
the customer segment you have defined.

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:53.520
So, if I believe that my customer segment
are teenagers, and

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:55.780
I'm talking to my colleagues at Stanford
and

00:05:55.780 --> 00:06:00.330
sharing my idea with my colleagues at
Stanford, there seems alignment.

00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:02.860
If I'm targeting teenagers,

00:06:02.860 --> 00:06:07.429
the customers that I'm gonna be testing my
prototype with needs to be teenagers.

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:10.900
The third one is, how are you gonna reach
them?

00:06:10.900 --> 00:06:11.950
That's an interesting one.

00:06:11.950 --> 00:06:15.080
So, if my assumption is I'm gonna reach
them at the,

00:06:15.080 --> 00:06:20.020
at the mall, then try to go to the mall
